  "jobTitle": "Sr Software Engineer",
  "summary": "Senior Software Engineer with extensive experience in designing and developing automation frameworks, plugins, and cloud-integrated solutions using WPF, C#, .NET, and modern technologies. Skilled in building scalable, reusable systems, modernizing legacy software, and collaborating with cross-functional teams to deliver high-quality solutions.\n\nAutomation & Framework Development: Enhanced automation actions and triggers in WPF/C#; developed modules like Excel, PDF, Image, SNMP, Event, Clipboard, Timer, Screen Capture, Printer, Multimedia, ODS, and Session Actions.\n\nPlugin Architecture & COM Interop: Architected and developed a Plugin Factory leveraging registration-free COM for simplified deployment and maintainability.\n\nGUI & Front-End Development: Built front-end GUIs using WPF and MVVM, improving usability and workflow efficiency.\n\nCloud & Virtualization Technologies: Automated workflows using AWS, Azure, VMware vSphere, and Dynamic CRM; implemented Health Check report modules using Excel and XML.\n\nLegacy Modernization: Ported legacy action and trigger plug-ins to .NET with emphasis on low-level system features, including service and process management.\n\nAgile & Team Collaboration: Occasionally served as Scrum Master, coordinated internal builds and releases for QA, and supported customer-facing engineers.\n\nInternship Experience: Designed test cases and automation for cloud, VMware, SharePoint, FTP, and Microsoft Azure; developed Human Detection Motion Detection software at IPR, India.\n\nTechnical Skills:\n\nLanguages: C#, XAML, C, C++, Java, HTML, Prolog, XML, PHP\n\nDatabases: SQL Server, Oracle, PostgreSQL, MS Access\n\nApplications/Tools: MS Office, MS Visio, SharePoint 2007, VMware, Microsoft Azure, Dynamic CRM\n\nSpecialties: Object-Oriented Programming, Design Patterns, Component-Based and Distributed Systems, .NET Web Services\n\nKey Qualities:\n\nStrong analytical and problem-solving skills\n\nExcellent multitasker and team player\n\nWorks well under pressure to meet critical deadlines",
